{"ld": 1891, "paper": "HP1262", "session": "132", "title": "An Act to Address the Dental Professional Workforce Shortage by Establishing Scholarship and Loan Programs and Updating the Dental Care Access Tax Credit", "sponsor_id": "h-daigle-lucien", "cosponsor_ids": ["h-debrito-flavia", "h-graham-anne", "h-griffin-abigail", "h-lemelin-michael", "s-moore-marianne", "s-stewart-harold"], "committee_code": "EDU", "committee_name": "Education and Cultural Affairs", "summary": {"text": "This bill establishes the Dentists for Maine's Future Scholarship Program to provide a tuition subsidy of 50% of the cost of attendance, up to a maximum of $25,000 per student annually, for eligible students who enter dental school programs in this State for the purpose of increasing the number of dentists in this State who practice in extreme shortage areas of the State. The bill also establishes the Extreme Shortage Area Dental Education Loan Program to provide loans and loan repayment agreements to eligible dental students and individuals who are eligible for licensure as a doctor of dental medicine or as a dental hygienist, dental therapist, expanded function dental assistant or dental assistant who agrees to serve an extreme shortage area in the State. The bill also updates the dental care access tax credit to include eligible dental hygienists and changes the date that the tax credit is repealed to December 31, 2032.", "official": true, "source": "Bill text, https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP1262&item=1&snum=132"}, "status": "died", "status_label": "Ought Not to Pass Pursuant To Joint Rule 310", "final_disposition": {"label": "Ought Not to Pass Pursuant To Joint Rule 310", "date": "2025-05-20", "governor_action": null, "governor_action_date": null}, "fiscal_status": "Not Yet Determined", "documents": [{"label": "Bill text (LD 1891)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP1262&item=1&snum=132", "item": 1}], "amendments": [], "co